[{:db/id 17592186124509 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1fec2431-d065-5bba-8c18-02d476e1dc33" "question-28ec3dc9-c6d5-5b75-a09b-0f48f395ab8d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1fec2431-d065-5bba-8c18-02d476e1dc33" :question/id #uuid "1fec2431-d065-5bba-8c18-02d476e1dc33" :question/math-academy-id "q-74014" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+(y-1)^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}=1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+(y-1)^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+(y-1)^{2}-1 & =\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2} & =16(\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+(y-1)^{2}-1) \\\\ z & =\\pm 4\\sqrt{\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+(y-1)^{2}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+(y-1)^{2}-1 & \\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+(y-1)^{2} & \\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the exterior of the ellipse $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+(y-1)^{2}=1,$ which includes the boundary.\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+(y-1)^{2}\\ge 1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e4502bac-b95a-55f0-b8aa-e4531b3d53f1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e4502bac-b95a-55f0-b8aa-e4531b3d53f1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4502bac-b95a-55f0-b8aa-e4531b3d53f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ed3fc56b-37c5-55d4-9d7e-18c3f48790c1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ed3fc56b-37c5-55d4-9d7e-18c3f48790c1" "answer-c970f5ab-4e4d-5836-a7ea-bb38ca163641" "answer-6664498a-b8f5-59ab-b882-7ea3cc1260a3" "answer-647d79bc-f910-5f37-9518-15b28a26a365" "answer-e08b4887-48da-5258-b769-f2c5686179db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed3fc56b-37c5-55d4-9d7e-18c3f48790c1" :answer/id #uuid "ed3fc56b-37c5-55d4-9d7e-18c3f48790c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+(y-1)^{2}\\ge 1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c970f5ab-4e4d-5836-a7ea-bb38ca163641" :answer/id #uuid "c970f5ab-4e4d-5836-a7ea-bb38ca163641" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6664498a-b8f5-59ab-b882-7ea3cc1260a3" :answer/id #uuid "6664498a-b8f5-59ab-b882-7ea3cc1260a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-647d79bc-f910-5f37-9518-15b28a26a365" :answer/id #uuid "647d79bc-f910-5f37-9518-15b28a26a365" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e08b4887-48da-5258-b769-f2c5686179db" :answer/id #uuid "e08b4887-48da-5258-b769-f2c5686179db" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The entire $xy$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-28ec3dc9-c6d5-5b75-a09b-0f48f395ab8d" :question/id #uuid "28ec3dc9-c6d5-5b75-a09b-0f48f395ab8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-164302" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}=-1,$ find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9} & =-1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+1 & =\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9} & =(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+1 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =9((x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+1) \\\\ z & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+1\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is ${R}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2e07a855-54d3-5672-a263-c28fae61891d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2e07a855-54d3-5672-a263-c28fae61891d" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e07a855-54d3-5672-a263-c28fae61891d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cd42f6f5-8e5b-53dc-b5eb-fcddd900ecf8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fda21d60-b280-5d0d-beed-f16249e1a048" "answer-1947e7ad-9f28-5f1c-bbd7-0534d7ae56a8" "answer-4a717d1f-b7eb-5705-90ee-dc90eea2ac01" "answer-69b1c641-c4ea-5e70-b0c0-21d7aa7137c3" "answer-cd42f6f5-8e5b-53dc-b5eb-fcddd900ecf8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fda21d60-b280-5d0d-beed-f16249e1a048" :answer/id #uuid "fda21d60-b280-5d0d-beed-f16249e1a048" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}<1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1947e7ad-9f28-5f1c-bbd7-0534d7ae56a8" :answer/id #uuid "1947e7ad-9f28-5f1c-bbd7-0534d7ae56a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}>1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a717d1f-b7eb-5705-90ee-dc90eea2ac01" :answer/id #uuid "4a717d1f-b7eb-5705-90ee-dc90eea2ac01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}\\ge 1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69b1c641-c4ea-5e70-b0c0-21d7aa7137c3" :answer/id #uuid "69b1c641-c4ea-5e70-b0c0-21d7aa7137c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}\\le 1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd42f6f5-8e5b-53dc-b5eb-fcddd900ecf8" :answer/id #uuid "cd42f6f5-8e5b-53dc-b5eb-fcddd900ecf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-88792370-e4b5-529c-9775-596955ef5e16" :activity/id #uuid "88792370-e4b5-529c-9775-596955ef5e16" :activity/ti